// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// CROWN — a handler's config DEFAULT performs where the arms perform: at
// the install, in the installer's world. So a default that performs E must
// reach the installer's row and meet its `!E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// SEEN RED at pin b9733815b54d — the pin that closed the same leak one
// field over, for state inits. The defaults were still judged before
// r_handle's scope opened, so this checked CLEAN with T_OverDeclared
// reporting the body "only uses Pure" while the default genuinely
// performed: give `op` a handler returning 7 and the value arrives at `k`.
//
// One rule, two carriers: everything the install EVALUATES belongs in
// row(h), which the tee already adds to every installer.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { g() -> Int }
handler hf(k: Int = op()) with s = 1 {
  g() => resume(s + k),
}
fn bad() with !E = (g()) ~> hf
fn main() = bad()
